From 20508baaa79586dec3fac5fe84e9e1860fc8af14 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: sysretq0 <sysretq0@proton.me>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 03:10:47 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 63/65] net: wwan: mtk_ccci: Add ccci_aud speech bridge, system
 RX, DPMAIF PM and shutdown

Prepare the MT6789 CCCI transport for full modem bring-up (data, voice,
SMS, and VoLTE):

- Add /dev/ccci_aud (CCIF0 Q0 ch=4 RX / ch=5 TX, PORT_F_USER_HEADER) to
  bridge Gen95 speech mailbox and payload packets between userspace and
  MD1 while dropping boot-time speech hello frames when no daemon is open.
- Handle CCCI_CH_SYSTEM_RX (ch=2) system notifications and quietly drain
  CCCI_CH_IMSDC_DL (ch=59) to eliminate unhandled-channel boot warnings.
- Add defensive DPMAIF suspend/resume hooks that save DL_L2TIMR0 and
  restore DL/UL interrupt masks and HW UL rings if DPMAIF PD loses power.
- Wire a platform .shutdown callback to quiesce CCIF/DPMAIF IRQs and
  WWAN interfaces cleanly on reboot without powering off live MD MTCMOS.

Signed-off-by: sysretq0 <sysretq0@proton.me>

